   "id": "pesachim.88a.15",
   "daf": "88a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "עֶבֶד שֶׁל שְׁנֵי שׁוּתָּפִין וְכוּ׳. רָמֵי לֵיהּ רַב עֵינָא סָבָא לְרַב נַחְמָן: תְּנַן, עֶבֶד שֶׁל שְׁנֵי שׁוּתָּפִין לֹא יֹאכַל מִשֶּׁל שְׁנֵיהֶן. וְהָתַנְיָא: רָצָה — מִזֶּה אוֹכֵל, רָצָה — מִזֶּה אוֹכֵל!",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «A slave» jointly owned «by two partners» may not eat from the lamb of either of them unless it was stipulated beforehand from whose lamb he will partake. «Rav Eina the Elder raised a contradiction before Rav Naḥman. We learned» in the mishna: «A slave» jointly owned «by two partners» may not eat from the lamb of either of them. «But wasn’t it taught» in a baraita: If «he wanted» to, «he» may «eat from this» one, and if «he wanted» to, «he» may «eat from that» one?"
  }
